Z||000000||88 Database Nut||10-08-2001||12:37 PM||||Guys and Gals,<P>This Saturday, Ed Parks will be picking up the 1985 Blue SE from my house in Marietta Georgia.  As most of you no doubt know, he is going to take this rare car and restore it to factory fresh condition.  We are still researching it's history, but it seems clear it was a special car produced to test the shade of blue used in the 1987 model year cars.  <P>Anyway, I thought that it would be nice to have the Club meet at my house this Saturday, to meet Ed and Rosey and let him see what our club looks like.  I'll be grilling burgers and hotdogs, and there will be some sort of refreshments (Ramon, how's the homebrew coming along?).  If anybody is interested in coming over for this, drop me an email at the address below so I can get a idea of how many people we're talking about.  This would be a good time for anyone who hasn't met Ed and Rosey yet to come on over!  You don't have to be a club member to come, just let me know ahead of time.  I will email people with directions.  I know there is a club cruise to Macon planned for this weekend, so if people can't come over I understand.  If the club people could tell the other club members who don't have internet access, I would be grateful.  I will also post this to the club bulletin board later today.<P>Hope to see you this Saturday,<P>John Willhoff john.willhoff@LMCO.com, jwwillhoff@aol.com, 770-578-6556||||reg||4
Z||000001||jch82||10-08-2001||02:50 PM||||Awww, I wanna come! Ed and Rosy are so nice!! I can't wait to go down there to have my 3.4 put in. It's a shame Georgia is sooo far away. Tell 'em Ken and I said HI. Thanks<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jch82flag.jpg"> ||||reg||7
